    <description>LFRDN-606: deactivated. Business decided to stop automatic round-robin assignment — leads now route to the BU queue (AF_AR_Lead_Routing, unchanged) and are assigned to a specific agent by the CRM Manager/Supervisor, not auto-rotated or self-assigned. See AF_VR_Lead_OwnerAssignByManagerOnly. Left in Draft rather than deleted so the rotation logic and Round_Robin_Assignment__c pointer records aren&apos;t lost if this is ever revisited.

Assigns new Leads directly to a rotating member of the target BU&apos;s Lead Queue, instead of leaving them queue-owned until someone manually claims one. Uses the roundRobinAssigner package (ported from the Palm Hills org 16 Aug 2026) — the Round_Robin_Assignment__c record tracks the rotation pointer per Queue.

Business Unit is derived inline via AF_FL_Sub_DeriveBusinessUnit rather than reading AF_BusinessUnit__c, since that field is written by a separate after-save flow whose execution order relative to this one is not guaranteed.

Suppressed-duplicate Leads (AF_IsSuppressedDuplicate__c = true) always route to the Review queue&apos;s rotation, regardless of Brand/BU, matching AF_AR_Lead_Routing&apos;s own priority order.</description>
